# Repair plan for /jest/jest:tests.unit.greeting.test.js::greet_greets_the_world_when_no_name_is_given

## Diagnosis

`services/greeter/greeting.js` declares:

```
function greet(name) {
  return 'Hello, ' + name + '!';
}
```

When `greet()` is called with no argument, `name` is `undefined` and string concatenation stringifies it, producing `"Hello, undefined!"`. The failing test calls `greet()` with no argument and asserts `"Hello, world!"`. The file's own header comment states the contract: *"greet greets a person by name, and the world when no name is given"* — the missing default is the planted defect, and it is in production source, inside the only declared write root (`services/greeter`, per `docs/architecture/architecture.yaml`).

No harness, config, or test change is involved. `tests/jest.config.js`, `tests/stack-frames.js`, and `tests/unit/canary.test.js` are all healthy and must be left untouched.

