An equivalent explicit guard inside the body (fall back to `'world'` when the argument is not provided) is acceptable if the writer prefers it, as long as a supplied name is never overridden. Keep the change minimal and local: one function signature or one fallback expression. Do not introduce new modules, new exports, config files, dependencies, or a `package.json` under `services/greeter` — none are needed, and `transform: {}` means the file is loaded by Node as-is (default parameters are natively supported by any Node version that runs this Jest install, so no transpilation concern arises).

